    <description><![CDATA[<h1 id="whoami" class="headerLink">
    <a href="#whoami" class="header-mark"></a>whoami</h1><p>My name is Mathilde and I&rsquo;m a former <strong>illustrator</strong> 🎨 now working in <strong>information security</strong>.</p>
<p>Computers always attracted me (I discovered and used Ubuntu for the first time at age 12 🤓). Thanks to <a href="https://www.42network.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">School 42</a>, a free-tuition computer programming school in Paris, I could make a bold career change and become an OSINT tools developer! Strange but true: I enjoy writing <a href="https://blog.lexfo.fr/infostealer-parser.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">parsers</a>.</p>
<blockquote>
  <p>💙 I love CTI, OSINT/investigative journalism, recreational pentesting (Portswigger Web Academy, <a href="https://www.root-me.org/maty4" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Root Me</a>) <a href="/ctf/" rel="">CTFs</a>, and especially learning new things (currently focusing on <strong>reverse engineering</strong>).</p>]]></description>
